**Rule (First-class LC angular-frequency output)** · `rule:matrix:lc-angular-frequency-output`

`LcAngularFrequencyPublication` consumes a sealed original bindings definition and the existing native `LcSpectrum`/`LcRootJacobian` path. `Heap::publish_lc_angular_frequency` targets the exact physical law at the original represented L/C center, with an explicit source-free radian relation and exact angular-frequency kind. Retain the ordered selections, original model/source identities and zero-block assumptions, operating points and policy, checked symbolic derivative, numerical Jacobian centers/errors, covariance and its own numerical error, deterministic total/numerical channels and all dependency versions. Predeclare the value and ordered companions, publish their connected bundle atomically, and reject any stale source, companion or output even after an equal-value write. The result keeps inherited `LinearizedMoments` and grants no nonlinear mean, finite nonlinear moments or distributional validity. The exact nominal analytic formula and the quantity composition at its actual rounded intermediate points are separate oracle targets. Both-format evidence must cover reference/varied inputs, common-source and fixed twins, missing source/model/block refusals, kind/role/full-box changes, cold/warm and late-publication literal `N`/`N−1` limits with consumed prefixes, and retirement. `PublishedLcAngularFrequency` lends the original center, numerical partials, covariance parameter and error, model and assurance only after validating the entire connected bundle. The heap group itself retains the original definition and numerical proof, including when the result wrapper is dropped. The quantity example remains a separate composition (`ex:matrix:quantity-covariance-lc-resonance`).

**Rule (Connected LC cyclic-frequency output)** · `rule:matrix:lc-cyclic-frequency-output`

The cyclic extension shall consume the retained ω₀ output evidence through the explicit full-cycle relation `f₀ = ω₀/(2π rad)`, without recomputing the LC root. Its sealed definition retains the original L/C declarations and positive-domain correspondence, the one-radian and full-cycle meanings, ordered output/companion symbols and distinct exact angular/cyclic frequency kinds. Certify the source-free coefficient `a_f = 1/(2π rad)` with its own numerical error. For the inherited local model retain `J_f = a_f J_ω`, `U_f = a_f² U_ω`, `Cov(ω₀,f₀) = a_f U_ω` and, for each requested retained output g, `Cov(f₀,g) = a_f Cov(ω₀,g)` with the matching right-axis factor for the transpose. Each covariance and Jacobian parameter carries its own numerical error. Scale total and numerical-only radii by the absolute coefficient enclosure and add coefficient-evaluation and result-rounding discrepancies to the appropriate channel, counting numerical error once inside a complete total. Coefficient error supplies no statistical source or physical variance.

Publish the requested connected ω₀/f₀ values, covariance blocks, parameter errors and deterministic companions in one transaction with no observable prefix on refusal; any source, companion or output write retires that bundle. Preserve the original joint model, known/declared-zero/unknown block assumptions, operating points and policy, checked sensitivity and every live version. The native consumer retains the exact physical law at the original represented L/C center; the separate quantity chain retains its actual rounded intermediate points. Inherit `LinearizedMoments` without asserting a nonlinear mean, finite nonlinear moments or model adequacy. Required evidence distinguishes the exact nominal `1000/π Hz` reference from represented-center and retained-composition targets, checks frequency/period inverse relations, both covariance axes and full-cycle/sign/target mutations in both formats, and pairs unsupported-factor and atomic resource refusals with acceptance at literal `N`/`N−1` Work/storage limits including consumed prefixes. The closed native implementation is `LcFrequencyPublication` with `Heap::publish_lc_frequency`; the angular publisher remains available for an angular-only result (`rule:matrix:lc-angular-frequency-output`), (`rule:matrix:quantity-conversion-routing`), (`rule:matrix:lc-frequency-bundle-publication`).

