`LcSourceBinding` joins both bindings-checked `ReadingSourceMap` targets to the existing `LcSpectrum` and evaluated original `ReciprocalDerivativeEvaluation`. The physical L/C input contract remains scalar identity-coordinate readings; their complete source ancestry may include mapped, signed, repeated and copied family coordinates or checked overlaps. Admission matches the original source bindings through both native joint targets, retains original source order and native model-column correspondence, checks complete covariance blocks and refuses independently imported equal-center substitutions. It shares `LcRootJacobian` and the existing implicit-root numerical partials, with the existing strict positive full-box evaluation. `Heap::evaluate_lc_source_statistics` composes the two maps with the original partials and exposes complete typed 8-by-8 operator/root covariance and original-source sensitivity columns. Exact real zeros and opposite root signs are retained. Every parameter access rechecks original selected sources, physical targets, the native joint declaration and arithmetic revision. No generic heap root moment companion is attached, no nonlinear mean or physical support is claimed, and original uncertain L/C-to-driven-reactance remains separate.

Both formats independently contract singular and full-rank correlated factors, retaining the source order and both signed maps across stored-copy and overlapping-alias selections (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-original-order-and-cross-blocks`), (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-mapped-copied-overlapping-models`). Missing cross blocks, equal-center imported sources, stale originals and selected-copy substitutions refuse (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-identity-and-version-refusals`), (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-refuses-substituted-selected-copy`). Omitted physical derivative directions keep `SpectralLawError::Transport` (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-retains-fixed-direction-refusal`). This separately allocated adapter leaves the native two-column and quantity resource pins unchanged; its scoped owners have their own literal boundaries (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-literal-owner-boundaries`). General nonidentity physical L/C input lowering, generic `MomentRef` attachment and driven nonlinear lineage retain distinct boundaries.

