Scalar identity readings of expanded families can be imported when all original scalar coordinates are present in the same import and exact rational evaluation of the affine ancestry agrees with every represented selected value. Finite IEEE values are decoded to integer significands and powers of two for this consistency check; no floating premise enters the CAS graph. Missing original coordinates and inconsistent repeated or negative copies refuse before publication. Existing complete Complex-block admission remains unchanged. The new exact-copy route refuses every companion targeted at a copied reading as `LiveBindingError::Heap(HeapError::MissingCoverage)`: exact center agreement does not establish propagation of original deterministic or numerical-error radii. Companion-free copies retain `RepresentedInputs` coverage even when originals have radius companions. Both formats refuse an understated copy radius before publication and retry without copy companions on the same capacity-limited heap (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-refuses-copy-companions`). General rounded affine-copy discrepancy coverage and partial writes to expanded families remain unsupported (`test:integration:lc-source-composition-exact-copy-admission`).

