`LcSourceBinding::spectrum` exposes its original immutable spectral plan for separate scheduling. `Heap::evaluate_lc_source_statistics_reusing` consumes a completed deterministic evaluation only from that same plan owner. The existing source-binding admission continues to refuse statistical spectral extensions; this entry point does not broaden that boundary. It revalidates the evaluation and every original source/model/target before using the retained normalized root and keeps its original receipts in the result. Equal-valued independent plans and foreign heaps cannot supply this authority. The numerical-only root radius is reconstructed outward about the retained center and supplies the implicit derivative denominator with the original time reference; the original evaluated operator partials still supply its numerator. This route calls neither the spectral evaluator nor another square root. A symmetric retained root enclosure that reaches zero refuses without a recomputation fallback, even when a separately requested cold evaluation could succeed.

