**Rule (Closed reusable spectral family)** · `rule:matrix:lc-spectral-batch`

`LcSpectralSchema` authenticates one original checked LC law and exports its exact constants once. Each `bind` checks the actual original L/C meanings, identity maps, complete companion selections and heap versions. Binary32 and binary64 bindings share the immutable schema while retaining their separate numerical owners. `LcSpectralBatch` prepares a finite insertion-ordered key index and stable point table before executing the source-free coefficient node and later autonomous root stratum. One fixed coefficient array is decoded once for the common arithmetic/schema key; every compatible root borrows it. Its closed dependency projection is the original semantic schema, literal/precision/arithmetic policy and both complete L/C bindings; it has no frequency or RHS input and no decision continuation. The same schema produces independently checked results for several positive L/C instances in both formats (`test:integration:lc-spectral-batch-rebinds-one-schema`).

