Each invariant has one execution attempt and one inline result/status slot. Rows reference its original complete evaluation; adapters must consume that evaluation's original `plan()`. No child ledger resets cumulative Work. A resource refusal leaves a named blocked suffix, and a consumed attempt cannot retry with a new ledger (`test:integration:lc-spectral-batch-cumulative-attempt`). Domain, binding and numerical failures retain their own outcomes beside independent successes (`test:integration:lc-spectral-batch-retains-independent-outcomes`). Current result access revalidates every original source and radius channel and active owner allowances; the original conservative whole-graph fallback remains in force for these `WholeBase` sources, and historical success alone grants no live authority (`test:integration:lc-spectral-batch-revalidates-all-channels`).

